window.EN={"1":"Seeking one of the \"Divine Weapons,\" Roy and the others advance their army toward the ruins on the Sacae plains.","2":"But there, survivors of the Djute tribe that Roy and the others once defeated","3":"had set a trap and lay in wait for them.","4":"The Etrurian lot are attacking!","5":"Are they trying to make even this place their own, to the very end...?","6":"We won't let them. Send word to our brothers too.","7":"We will defend this place to the death without fail. We'll avenge the Djute tribe's grudge.","8":"Yes, sir!","9":"※If Shin is deployed","10":"So this is where a \"Divine Weapon\" is...","11":"Shin, did you know about this place?","12":"...I've heard of it.","13":"The bow used by the \"Divine Knight\" Hanon,","14":"the \"Gale Bow\" Murgleis, is said to be kept here.","15":"Hanon... I've heard the only two women ever given","16":"the title of \"Eight Generals\" were the Saint Elimine and Hanon.","17":"So it seems.","18":"...You should be careful.","19":"Those guarding this place are survivors of the Djute tribe.","20":"They'll see us as their mortal enemy and come at us with everything they have.","21":"Got it. Let's keep our guard up!","22":"※If Shin is not deployed, and Dayan is deployed","23":"So this is where a \"Divine Weapon\" is...","24":"Dayan, do you know about this place?","25":"Of course.","26":"The bow used by the \"Divine Knight\" Hanon is kept here.","27":"The weapon Hanon used was the \"Gale Bow\" Murgleis...","28":"At least, that's what I heard from Elffin.","29":"So that's what you call it over where you're from.","30":"Being a woman, the one given the title of \"Eight Generals\"","31":"is said to be the two of them, the Saint Elimine and Hanon.","32":"I see.","33":"By the way, Lord Roy, you should be careful.","34":"Those guarding this place are survivors of the Djute tribe.","35":"They'll see us as their mortal enemy and come at us with everything they have.","36":"Got it. Let's keep our guard up!","37":"※If Shin and Dayan are not deployed, and Sue is deployed","38":"So this is where a \"Divine Weapon\" is...","39":"Sue, did you know about this place?","40":"...Only by rumor.","41":"I hear the bow Hanon used is kept here.","42":"Hanon, you mean the \"Divine Knight,\" right?","43":"Then that bow would be the \"Gale Bow\" Murgleis...","44":"I don't know its name.","45":"You don't know? Even though it's the weapon an \"Eight General\" used?","46":"It's all the same no matter who used it. A name is nothing but a vessel.","47":"Isn't it enough to \"know\" the thing itself?","48":"...I wonder about this bow, though.","49":"Do you think it's the one we call Murgleis?","50":"Yes, from what I've heard, there's no mistake.","51":"※If Shin, Dayan, and Sue are not deployed","52":"So this is where a \"Divine Weapon\" is...","53":"Elffin, did you find out anything about this place?","54":"...I looked into the legends of the Sacae region, and","55":"here, the bow used by the \"Divine Knight\" Hanon,","56":"the \"Gale Bow\" Murgleis, is said to be kept.","57":"Hanon... I've heard the only two women ever given","58":"the title of \"Eight Generals\" were the Saint Elimine and Hanon.","59":"Yes.","60":"...Lord Roy, those guarding this place are said to be survivors of the Djute tribe.","61":"They'll treat our army as their \"enemy\" and come at us with everything they have.","62":"Got it. Let's keep our guard up!","63":"※Only if you attacked the wrong place","64":"The enemy's fallen for the trap! Get them!","65":"We found it! A bow, on the altar inside the tent!","66":".........","67":"So this is... the \"Gale Bow\" Murgleis.","68":"...It looks like an ordinary bow, but","69":"surely it holds some tremendous power within it.","70":"Lord Roy.","71":"It seems the Bern soldiers who were nearby are fleeing.","72":"I see.","73":"\"I see\" isn't good enough. We must pursue them.","74":"No.","75":"They're trying to get away from the battlefield. They surely have no more will to fight.","76":"But still...","77":"Soldiers have families too. There's no need to fight them more than necessary.","78":"Marinas, I'd like you to send this letter to Bern's Priest Yodel.","79":"A letter...? May I ask what it says?","80":"It's something I heard from Niime. About the \"dragons\" Bern makes use of.","81":"Oh! Whatever sort of talk did you have?","82":"It would take a while to explain, so...","83":"I haven't sealed it yet, so it'd be best if you just read over the letter yourself.","84":"Understood. Well then, let me have a look right away...","85":"...Lord Roy.","86":"Princess Guinevere. Is something the matter?","87":"...From here on, it's Bern, isn't it.","88":"Yes, we'll finally be advancing our army into Bern's homeland.","89":"...So, this time, could I ask you to hear me out to the very end?","90":"...Yes. I came prepared to do just that.","91":"...At the time, Prince Zephiel, as Bern's heir,","92":"had grown up with nothing lacking, hadn't he.","93":"So I've heard.","94":"Even so, Bern's former king came to resent Prince Zephiel, didn't he?","95":"Rather... it's because my brother had grown so remarkably.","96":"Eh...","97":"My father, Bern's former king, was, as a king, a man of ordinary talent, they say.","98":"So my brother's outstanding talent seems to have only made Father's feelings all the colder.","99":".........","100":"And then, one day at last, Father is said to have called my brother and told him:","101":"\"Someone fit for it shall be brought in to marry Guinevere, and he shall take Bern's throne.\"","102":"What...! ...That's too much!","103":"Even so, my brother is said to have answered then that if that was how it was, so be it.","104":"But to my brother, who everyone expected to be the next king, those around him would not allow such a thing.","105":"And so, Father, driven to distraction...","106":"...Plotted to assassinate Prince Zephiel?","107":"...At a drinking banquet, my brother was handed a poisoned cup directly by our father the king.","108":"And that, it's said, was the first and last cup he ever received from Father...","109":"After returning to his room, my brother began to suffer,","110":"and for more than ten days after that, he is said to have hovered between life and death.","111":"He was sheltered by General Murdock, who had raised him,","112":"and somehow, my brother's life was spared.","113":"...Did Father do nothing after that?","114":"...No.","115":"He treated General Murdock, who had saved my brother, and my brother's mother as obstacles too,","116":"and is said to have schemed to do away with my brother along with them.","117":"My brother, still bedridden with illness, learned of this and feigned his own death...","118":"...and when Father came to confirm my brother's death, from within the coffin... with a sword...","119":".........","120":"...At the time, I was still young, and had no way of understanding such circumstances.","121":"All I understood was that from that day—the day Father died—onward, my brother's face lost its smile.","122":"Until then, he could be strict, but he was a warm, gentle brother. That's why...","123":"Princess Guinevere...","124":"That's why, deep in my heart, I believed my brother hadn't changed.","125":"That someday, surely, he would return to being the kind Zephiel brother he once was.","126":"I believed that... I kept believing that, all along...","127":"I see, so that's how it was...","128":"...But now, my brother is somewhere my voice can no longer reach.","129":"Lord Roy, I beg you. Please... please stop my brother.","130":"Please make him stop tormenting Bern and the people of other regions any further.","131":"Even if it means appealing to the sword?","132":"...Ever since I entrusted everything to Lord Roy, I've made up my mind to it.","133":"Understood. I will definitely stop King Zephiel!","134":"I swear it on the \"Fire Emblem\" entrusted to me by the princess!"};
